 "voice": [
  {
   "id": "vo01",
   "t": 0.03333333333333333,
   "dur": 3.204,
   "file": "vo/01.wav",
   "text": "How fast are you moving now? Sitting perfectly still."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo02",
   "t": 4.033333333333333,
   "dur": 8.066,
   "file": "vo/02.wav",
   "text": "Earth spins: at the equator, the ground moves about sixteen hundred seventy kilometers an hour. That beats the speed of sound."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo03",
   "t": 13.1,
   "dur": 7.896,
   "file": "vo/03.wav",
   "text": "And Earth circles the Sun at about thirty kilometers every second. Since this began, you've gone farther than New York to Boston."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo04",
   "t": 21.633333333333333,
   "dur": 15.197,
   "file": "vo/04.wav",
   "text": "Ptolemy argued that if Earth moved, birds and clouds would be left behind. In sixteen thirty-two, Galileo answered with a ship's cabin. Below deck on calm water, nothing tells you the ship is moving. You feel a jolt, never a smooth ride."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo05",
   "t": 39.233333333333334,
   "dur": 12.284,
   "file": "vo/05.wav",
   "text": "Zoom out. The Sun drags us round the galaxy at about two hundred thirty kilometers a second. One lap: about two hundred thirty million years. Last time round, the first dinosaurs had just appeared."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo06",
   "t": 55.233333333333334,
   "dur": 4.266,
   "file": "vo/06.wav",
   "text": "So your speed has no single answer. First ask: compared to what?"
  },
  {
   "id": "vo07",
   "t": 60.03333333333333,
   "dur": 8.14,
   "file": "vo/07.wav",
   "text": "Light time, across your galactic trip so far: about a twentieth of a second. To the galaxy's center: about twenty-seven thousand years."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo08",
   "t": 69.1,
   "dur": 3.705,
   "file": "vo/08.wav",
   "text": "Next: more trees on Earth, or stars in our galaxy?"
  }
 ]
}